A-P2-04 correction evidence

The prior fragment measurements were n 1.21 mm ×3, a 14.87 mm, and H 1.19 mm. The defect was the start detector: it read black pixels from the dot as the first-stroke start. It did not inspect letter ink.

The corrected check loads the compiled week 1 HTML from `render(shipped())`. It uses the same local fonts, CSS, and page size as the print build. Its Chrome pipeline loads Paged.js, waits for fonts, runs `PagedPolyfill.preview()`, then sets print media. The browser context uses `deviceScaleFactor: 300 / 96`. The check takes screenshots of each real trace box, not isolated HTML fragments. Gray glyph pixels are restricted to 153–204. Dot pixels are restricted to <=60. The first-stroke start is the top row of the left stem for n and H, and the top row of the right stem for a. It converts 300-dpi pixels to millimeters and keeps the 1.5 mm limit.

Corrected HEAD gaps: n 1 = 4.51 mm; n 2 = 4.59 mm; n 3 = 4.51 mm; a = 14.14 mm; H = 4.50 mm. The three n gaps agree within 1 mm with the proof v5 raster cross-check: page 4, `/tmp/opencode/print-check-2e/p4-top-300-04.png`, first trace box x 198–442, dot center about (243,1168), and left-stem start near x 283, y 1160; estimated gap about 4 mm. Moving the five dots onto the detected gray starts passes at 1.22, 1.22, 1.22, 1.27, and 1.27 mm.

