Type-fix correction facts

The type failure reported for commit `7f5eb435` was `TS2339: Property 'targetSelector' does not exist on type '{ selector: string; letter: string; rightStem: boolean; } | { selector: string; targetSelector: string; letter: string; rightStem: boolean; }'` at test lines 1481 and 1492. The cause was that `PROJECT_CHECKS`, including `npx tsc --noEmit`, was not run after the dot-test commit.

The fix declares one array type: `{ selector: string; targetSelector?: string; letter: string; rightStem: boolean }[]`. It changes no selector, measure, limit, assertion, or runtime value. Fix commit: `bd5b94ed94cefc0cc27f1bd00d7543d0b6626fe1`, test file only.

